  "name": "LinkedIn Post Approval",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Topic: {{ $('On form submission1').first().json.Topic }}\n\nDraft post:\n\"\"\"\n{{ $json.output }}\n\"\"\"\n\nReview this draft against your standards and return the improved final post.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a strict LinkedIn editor. You improve posts; you never explain your changes.\n\nScore the draft privately out of 10 on each of these:\n1. Hook - does line one alone make a professional want to read on?\n2. Clarity - one main idea, short sentences, no jargon or filler.\n3. CTA - exactly one clear call to action (a question or an action), near the end.\n\nRewrite the weakest of the three. Then check the whole post against these hard rules and fix anything that fails:\n- 120-150 words\n- Line one is the hook\n- Exactly one call to action\n- At most 3 hashtags, on the last line\n- Plain text only (no markdown, no bold, no bullet symbols), at most 2 emojis\n- No invented statistics, quotes, names or personal stories\n- Stays on the given topic\n\nOutput rules: return ONLY the final post, ready to paste into LinkedIn.\nDo not include the scores, feedback, headings, notes or quotation marks."
        }
      },
